doc:sch-1-sec-57bf-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "57BF(2) Meaning of safety and security information" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Safety information, for a scheme vehicle, is information relating to any of the following systems installed in the vehicle, of a kind prescribed by the scheme rules:  (a) the hydrogen system;  (b) the high voltage system;  (c) the hybrid system;  (d) the electric propulsion system;  (e) another system prescribed by the scheme rules for the purposes of this paragraph." ;
    cof:pageNumber "11"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00054-sch-1-sec-57bf-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57BF(3) Meaning of safety and security information"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-57bf-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Security information, for a scheme vehicle, is information relating to any of the following systems installed in the vehicle, of a kind prescribed by the scheme rules:  (a) the vehicle’s mechanical and electrical security system;  (b) another system prescribed by the scheme rules for the purposes of this paragraph.  Schedule 1  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme" ;
    skos:definition "(3) Security information, for a scheme vehicle, is information relating to any of the following systems installed in the vehicle, of a kind prescribed by the scheme rules:  (a) the vehicle’s mechanical and electrical security system;  (b) another system prescribed by the scheme rules for the purposes of this paragraph.  Schedule 1  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9adccc772317e7ac32d2e4321973e993de5264c9e06b4d971ec45579b4db12b0" ;
