doc:sch-1-sec-57ca-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "57CA(5) Scheme information—offer to supply to Australian repairers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) For the purposes of subsection (4), this subsection covers the following matters:  (a) the price charged to other Australian repairers and scheme RTOs for supplying scheme information (whether under this Part or otherwise) in relation to a scheme vehicle:  (i) of that particular make, model and year; or  (ii) if pricing is not available for information in relation to a scheme vehicle of that particular make, model and year—pricing for information in relation to a scheme vehicle of a similar make, model and year;  (b) the terms and conditions on which such scheme information is offered for supply to Australian repairers and scheme RTOs (whether under this Part or otherwise), including as to the permitted use of the information, the means of access to the information, the number of permitted users, and the frequency or duration of use of the information;  (c) the anticipated demand by Australian repairers and scheme RTOs for supply of the scheme information on the basis of the scheme offer;  Schedule 1  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00054-sch-1-sec-57cb a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57CB Scheme information—supply on request by Australian"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-57cb ;
    values:originalText "repairers or scheme RTOs Scope  (1) This section applies if:  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 54, 2021 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Motor Vehicle Service and Repair Information Sharing Scheme) Act 2021  (a) a data provider makes, or is required to make, a scheme offer to supply scheme information in relation to a particular make, model and year of scheme vehicle; and  (b) either:  (i) an Australian repairer has a need to access the scheme information for that particular make, model and year of scheme vehicle in carrying on the Australian repairer’s business; or  (ii) a scheme RTO has a need to access the scheme information to provide an RTO course; and  (c) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO requests, in writing, the data provider to supply the scheme information about that particular make, model and year of scheme vehicle; and  (d) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay, the scheme price, or another agreed price, for the scheme information. Note: Restrictions apply in relation to the supply of scheme information that is safety and security information: see section 57DB. Supply of scheme information  (2) The data provider must supply the scheme information to the Australian repairer or scheme RTO:  (a) in accordance with terms and conditions that comply with section 57CC; and  (b)  within the period covered by subsection (3). Note: A pecuniary penalty of up to $10,000,000 may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection: see section 76.  (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the period covered by this subsection:  (a) starts when (at the payment or offer time) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay, the scheme price, or another agreed price, for the scheme information; and  (b) in the circumstances described in column 1 of an item of the following table, ends at the time described in column 2 of that item.   Schedule 1  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme" ;
    skos:definition "repairers or scheme RTOs Scope  (1) This section applies if:  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 54, 2021 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Motor Vehicle Service and Repair Information Sharing Scheme) Act 2021  (a) a data provider makes, or is required to make, a scheme offer to supply scheme information in relation to a particular make, model and year of scheme vehicle; and  (b) either:  (i) an Australian repairer has a need to access the scheme information for that particular make, model and year of scheme vehicle in carrying on the Australian repairer’s business; or  (ii) a scheme RTO has a need to access the scheme information to provide an RTO course; and  (c) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO requests, in writing, the data provider to supply the scheme information about that particular make, model and year of scheme vehicle; and  (d) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay, the scheme price, or another agreed price, for the scheme information. Note: Restrictions apply in relation to the supply of scheme information that is safety and security information: see section 57DB. Supply of scheme information  (2) The data provider must supply the scheme information to the Australian repairer or scheme RTO:  (a) in accordance with terms and conditions that comply with section 57CC; and  (b)  within the period covered by subsection (3). Note: A pecuniary penalty of up to $10,000,000 may be imposed for a contravention of this subsection: see section 76.  (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), the period covered by this subsection:  (a) starts when (at the payment or offer time) the Australian repairer or scheme RTO pays, or offers to pay, the scheme price, or another agreed price, for the scheme information; and  (b) in the circumstances described in column 1 of an item of the following table, ends at the time described in column 2 of that item.   Schedule 1  Motor vehicle serv"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ab7836a64cd786e0132dbb2166e58e9320e10181af86204a7cd35bf3d573ff65" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2021a00054-sch-1-sec-57cb-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2021a00054-sch-1-sec-57cb-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:c2021a00054-sch-1-sec-57cb-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2021a00054.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2021a00054.pdf, p.14" .
