concept:c2021a00054-sch-1-sec-57dd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57DD Safety and security information—storage of, and access to,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-57dd ;
    values:originalText "sensitive information Scope  (1) This section applies in relation to sensitive information if:  (a) the information is about an individual mentioned in paragraph 57DB(2)(a); and  (b) the information is obtained by a data provider for the purposes of determining whether the individual is a fit and  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 54, 2021 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Motor Vehicle Service and Repair Information Sharing Scheme) Act 2021  proper person to access and use safety and security information. Sensitive information must be stored in Australia  (2) If a data provider holds the sensitive information, the data provider must store the information in Australia or an external Territory. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units. Preventing access to sensitive information outside Australia  (3) A person must not do anything that might reasonably enable the sensitive information to be accessed outside Australia by the data provider, or any other person. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "sensitive information Scope  (1) This section applies in relation to sensitive information if:  (a) the information is about an individual mentioned in paragraph 57DB(2)(a); and  (b) the information is obtained by a data provider for the purposes of determining whether the individual is a fit and  Motor vehicle service and repair information sharing scheme  Schedule 1 Main amendments  Part 1  No. 54, 2021 Competition and Consumer Amendment (Motor Vehicle Service and Repair Information Sharing Scheme) Act 2021  proper person to access and use safety and security information. Sensitive information must be stored in Australia  (2) If a data provider holds the sensitive information, the data provider must store the information in Australia or an external Territory. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units. Preventing access to sensitive information outside Australia  (3) A person must not do anything that might reasonably enable the sensitive information to be accessed outside Australia by the data provider, or any other person. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "af91ce84e2a23c3e60d1d2ecdf8d290ac3e3ce70730689163d7e3dc00fe5646f" ;
