    skos:definition "(2) If a data provider holds the sensitive information, the data provider must store the information in Australia or an external Territory. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units. Preventing access to sensitive information outside Australia"@en ;
