doc:sch-1-sec-57dd-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "57DD(2) Safety and security information—storage of, and access to," ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If a data provider holds the sensitive information, the data provider must store the information in Australia or an external Territory. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units. Preventing access to sensitive information outside Australia" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2021a00054-sch-1-sec-57dd-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "57DD(3) Safety and security information—storage of, and access to,"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-57dd-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A person must not do anything that might reasonably enable the sensitive information to be accessed outside Australia by the data provider, or any other person. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units." ;
    skos:definition "(3) A person must not do anything that might reasonably enable the sensitive information to be accessed outside Australia by the data provider, or any other person. Civil penalty:  (a) for a body corporate—1,500 penalty units; and  (b) for a person other than a body corporate—300 penalty units."@en ;
